# MOLE's OWN triangulation, cell by cell and slot by slot.
#
# Produced by MOLE 2 itself with MOLE_TETRA_DUMP=1 (ComplexComputation.cs), which
# writes one line per cell in Triangulation.Vertices order:
#     centroid.x centroid.y centroid.z  nNullAdjacency  isBoundary  volume  v0;v1;v2;v3
# Kept here are the first 500 cells with only the fields a port can reproduce
# without running the rest of the pipeline - centroid, null-neighbour count and
# the four vertices IN MOLE'S ORDER - plus a digest over all of them.
#
# The vertex ORDER is the point. Any correct Delaunay code reproduces the cell
# set; only MOLE's own incremental insertion reproduces which of the four
# vertices is V0. See vmdhole/NOTES/mole2-dh-triangulation.md.
